.TH CLProcessor 1 "2026 August 28" ""

.SH NAME
CLProcessor \- CPU plugin tester application of the CoreLAB framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clprocessor
[options]

.SH COPYRIGHT
CoreLAB is Copyright (C) 2026 by Pozsar Zsolt.

.SH DESCRIPTION
The CLProcessor application is the processor simulation component of the CoreLAB
modular framework. It is intended for simple, manual testing of CPU simulator
plugins. The program supports processor plugins implementing different CPU
architectures.
.PP
The program is designed for Windows and Unix-like operating systems.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d \-\-dir
Set plugin directory.
.TP
.B \-i \-\-ignore-help
Ignore missing help file or viewer.
.TP
.B \-h \-\-help
Show useable parameters.
.TP
.B \-v \-\-version
Show version and build information.

.SH OPERATION
.PP
.SS Plugin architecture
Processor plugins are provided as dynamically loadable shared libraries
containing the processor implementation and its exported entry points. After
loading a plugin, \fIclprocessor\fP resolves the required entry points and
creates an instance of the plugin's \fITCPU\fP descendant.
.PP
The base class for processor plugins is \fITCPU\fP. A concrete CPU
implementation derives from this class and implements the processor-specific
register handling, instruction execution, reset operation, and state management.
.PP
After loading a processor plugin, the application connects it to the test
system bus, displays its properties and registers, and provides basic processor
control and memory operations. The loaded processor communicates with the
emulated memory and I/O ports through the \fIISysBus\fP interface.
.PP
.SS Plugin interface
The processor plugin interface consists of the \fITCPU\fP class and the
exported plugin entry points.
.PP
The \fITCPU\fP interface provides register access, execution control, reset,
interrupt requests, event notification, state saving and loading, and processor
identification and capability information.
.PP
.SS Minimal test environment
CLProcessor provides a minimal environment for testing processor plugins:
.TP
.IP \(bu 2
1 kB of Neumann or Harvard code memory.
.IP \(bu 2
1 kB of Harvard data memory.
.IP \(bu 2
One standard I/O port at address \fI$A0\fP. Its interrupt can be disabled.
.IP \(bu 2
One ASCII I/O console at address \fI$B0\fP. Its interrupt can be disabled.

The application also provides the following tools:
.IP \(bu 2
Memory examine and deposit.
.IP \(bu 2
Memory hexadecimal dump viewer (\fIHexViewer\fP).
.IP \(bu 2
Run logger (\fIRunLogger\fP), recording the instruction number, address, opcode
and mnemonic.
.IP \(bu 2
Memory content loading and saving in raw binary and Intel HEX formats.
.IP \(bu 2
Register viewer and editor.

.SH ENVIRONMENTAL VARIABLES
.TP
.B LANG
This is the system language on Unix-like operating systems.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B *.bin, *.hex:
Memory contents can be loaded from a bin or Intel hex file and saved to disk.
.TP
.B cpu_*.dll, libcpu_*.so :
The application loads processor plugins as shared libraries. On Windows,
plugins use the \fIcpu_*.dll\fP naming convention; on Unix-like systems,
\fIlibcpu_*.so\fP is used.
.TP
.B *.clpst:
Plugin state can be saved to and restored from CoreLAB stream files. The state
data is handled by the plugin through the corresponding state management
interface. Their content varies from plugin to plugin.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.

